00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:56.690
We've built this using a
[? when/if/then ?] engine.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:16:00.880
Let me show you what it
looks like for Team Drive.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:03.460
So here the IT admin is
building an onboarding workflow

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.170
for their sales department.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:08.110
So when a new sales rep or
when a new user is created

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:11.530
and they're added to
the sales org unit,

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.320
we're going to automate
a number of onboarding

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.357
related activities
for that user.

00:16:16.357 --> 00:16:18.190
Things like adding them
to the right groups,

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:21.040
sharing the right
calendars, and of course,

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.635
adding them to the
sales Team Drive.

00:16:23.635 --> 00:16:26.400
Now this completely
automates the process

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:29.460
of onboarding a user
into Team Drive,

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.180
but it also makes
sure that that user

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:37.860
has the access to everything
they need on day one.

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.780
And as you can see,
it's incredibly easy

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:43.860
to onboard your
users to Team Drive.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:46.930
Another thing that we
see a lot, team changes.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:49.020
Now let's say we
want to automate

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:52.620
the process of a user moving
from one team to another team.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:55.710
In this example, the user is
moving from the sales team

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:59.490
to the support team, and
this workflow completely

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:03.270
automates removing them
from the sales Team Drive

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:05.460
and adding them to the
support Team Drive.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.079
In addition to
this, it also adds

00:17:07.079 --> 00:17:09.750
them to support related
items and removes them

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.301
from sales related items, like
Slack channels or Slack user

00:17:13.301 --> 00:17:13.800
groups.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.349
And as you guys will see
later in this presentation,

00:17:16.349 --> 00:17:20.710
Slack has an amazing
Team Drive integration.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.800
And finally, these
actions can also

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:25.470
be taken one-off or in bulk.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:28.109
What we're looking at now
is the directory user grid

00:17:28.109 --> 00:17:29.370
in BetterCloud.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:35.490
I can filter by the
Department field in Google,

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:40.590
search specifically for sales,
and then via our action engine,

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:44.800
add them directly to Team Drive.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.710
To summarize,
BetterCloud empowers

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:50.860
IT to take action and
orchestrate complex processes

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:53.950
across your applications,
users, and data,

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:58.390
while ensuring accuracy,
precision, and compliance.

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:00.490
Every day, thousands
of customers

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:04.750
rely on BetterCloud to
centralize data and controls,

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.880
surface operational
intelligence,

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:10.150
and orchestrate complex
actions across all their SaaS

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.500
applications.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.080
And now you can too
with Team Drive.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:14.867
Thank you.

