company, a leader in Europe,

00:28:19.820 --> 00:28:24.250
with more than 13,000
employees on G Suite.

00:28:24.250 --> 00:28:28.210
We [? embolden ?] them two
years ago from their old custom

00:28:28.210 --> 00:28:33.250
made intranet and had to
move more than 1,000 pages

00:28:33.250 --> 00:28:38.830
to LumApps and thousands of
documents to Google Drive.

00:28:38.830 --> 00:28:43.930
And we now serve more than
10,000 pages every day

00:28:43.930 --> 00:28:45.340
for them.

00:28:45.340 --> 00:28:49.180
And even with these impressive
numbers of pages and employees,

00:28:49.180 --> 00:28:53.590
LumApps currently has
an 80% satisfaction rate

00:28:53.590 --> 00:28:56.250
on the quality of the site.

00:28:56.250 --> 00:29:00.540
However, they wanted to simplify
the permissions management

00:29:00.540 --> 00:29:03.270
on the drive assets,
and they also

00:29:03.270 --> 00:29:07.170
wanted to centralize the
ownership of all the files

00:29:07.170 --> 00:29:09.720
that are put on the intranet.

00:29:09.720 --> 00:29:13.420
And then, come Teams Drives.

00:29:13.420 --> 00:29:17.320
As lot of Google products,
Drive is deeply integrated

00:29:17.320 --> 00:29:18.580
in LumApps.

00:29:18.580 --> 00:29:21.280
And today, we are
proud to announce

00:29:21.280 --> 00:29:26.530
that the LumApps Drive features
now fully support Team Drives.

00:29:26.530 --> 00:29:30.730
From a technical perspective,
the journey was a pleasant one

00:29:30.730 --> 00:29:33.400
as the Team Drive
team was motivated

00:29:33.400 --> 00:29:35.530
to make sure the
API is backwards

00:29:35.530 --> 00:29:39.850
compatible and
well-documented and all teams

00:29:39.850 --> 00:29:41.680
worked well together.

00:29:41.680 --> 00:29:48.070
So we only add to make our
integrations Team Drive aware.

00:29:48.070 --> 00:29:51.850
So at LumApps we assembled a
team of two software engineers

00:29:51.850 --> 00:29:56.770
who corroborated with the
Team Drive experts at Google

00:29:56.770 --> 00:29:59.200
and they remain available 24/7.

00:29:59.200 --> 00:30:01.830
And we are especially
grateful for [? Birken ?]

00:30:01.830 --> 00:30:04.270
and [INAUDIBLE]
involvements, as well

00:30:04.270 --> 00:30:09.130
as are recommended for G Suite
team support with [INAUDIBLE].

00:30:09.130 --> 00:30:11.740
They helped us
with documentation

00:30:11.740 --> 00:30:14.920
and provided assistance
on the few hiccups

00:30:14.920 --> 00:30:16.720
we discovered with the API.

00:30:20.090 --> 00:30:23.570
So now let's focus on how we
solved our customers' issues,

00:30:23.570 --> 00:30:26.450
including Dalkia's.

00:30:26.450 --> 00:30:29.180
First, in LumApps,
we have widgets

00:30:29.180 --> 00:30:34.960
to embed and browse Team
Drives directly on any site.

00:30:34.960 --> 00:30:38.150
So these widgets are also
used for basic operation,

00:30:38.150 --> 00:30:43.490
like uploading files, creating
folders, moving files, and all

00:30:43.490 --> 00:30:47.870
of this in an effort to
encourage the usage of Drive

00:30:47.870 --> 00:30:48.970
all over the company.

00:30:53.230 --> 00:30:56.815
Next, in the search
engine, what we do

00:30:56.815 --> 00:31:01.090
is that we aggregate data
from the sites, the user

00:31:01.090 --> 00:31:06.220
directory, events, from
calendar, emails from Gmail.

00:31:06.220 --> 00:31:11.020
And so we also plugged the
search engine into Team Drives

00:31:11.020 --> 00:31:14.380
so users can quickly
find information

00:31:14.380 --> 00:31:16.520
from all their corporate data.

00:31:20.640 --> 00:31:23.130
And finally, all
team communities

00:31:23.130 --> 00:31:25.710
are a perfect fit
for Team Drive.

00:31:25.710 --> 00:31:29.970
They offer a place for
a team to share ideas,

00:31:29.970 --> 00:31:33.480
best practices to
manage a project,

00:31:33.480 --> 00:31:36.310
and so employees
can ask questions.

00:31:36.310 --> 00:31:39.690
They can share
files, plan events

00:31:39.690 --> 00:31:44.190
in a dedicated and fully
managed Team Drive and calendar.

00:31:44.190 --> 00:31:46.320
So the Team Drive
is automatically

00:31:46.320 --> 00:31:49.290
accessible to all
community members,

00:31:49.290 --> 00:31:52.920
and permissions are
synchronized as soon as you add

00:31:52.920 --> 00:31:55.620
the team members in LumApps.

00:31:55.620 --> 00:31:59.130
And this is a big relief
for our customer, Dalkia,

00:31:59.130 --> 00:32:02.910
as they can now focus on
collaboration and content

00:32:02.910 --> 00:32:04.725
creation.

00:32:04.725 --> 00:32:06.600
Well, if you want to
know more about LumApps,

00:32:06.600 --> 00:32:09.420
you can meet with
us at our booth,

00:32:09.420 --> 00:32:12.000
it's E12 at the
[? Moscone. ?] Or you

00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:14.590
can attend our customer
testimonial tomorrow

00:32:14.590 --> 00:32:17.240
with Veolia at 2:30 PM.

00:32:17.240 --> 00:32:18.522
Thank you.

00:32:18.522 --> 00:32:21.378
[APPLAUSE]

00:32:23.770 --> 00:32:24.609
STEVE BAZYL: Great.

00:32:24.609 --> 00:32:25.150
Thanks, Elie.

00:32:25.150 --> 00:32:27.970
As you can see, Team
Drives and the Drive API's

00:32:27.970 --> 00:32:30.130
already allowing
our partners to add

00:32:30.130 --> 00:32:31.670
a lot of valuable new services.

00:32:31.670 --> 00:32:33.940
But of course, we're
really excited about stuff

00:32:33.940 --> 00:32:37.930
that we haven't even seen yet
in terms of new use cases,

00:32:37.930 --> 00:32:40.720
and we're really excited to
see what people come up with.

00:32:43.342 --> 00:32:45.310
HODIE MEYERS: Yes, one
of those forward looking

00:32:45.310 --> 00:32:49.850
and completely
new use cases will

00:32:49.850 --> 00:32:51.672
be presented here by Salman.

00:32:51.672 --> 00:32:52.880
Salman, tell us all about it.

00:32:52.880 --> 00:32:53.921
SALMAN SUHAIL: Thank you.

00:32:53.921 --> 00:32:56.424
Thank you very much, Hodie.

00:32:56.424 --> 00:32:57.590
So my name is Salman Suhail.

00:32:57.590 --> 00:33:00.980
I'm a Senior Product Manager
at Slack on the platform team

00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:05.000
there, and I'm super
excited to be here today.

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:08.720
So at Slack-- and
everyone in this room

00:33:08.720 --> 00:33:11.600
is pretty aware that there's
a massive shift happening

00:33:11.600 --> 00:33:13.077
in the way that
work is happening

00:33:13.077 --> 00:33:15.410
and the way that businesses
are operating their software

00:33:15.410 --> 00:33:16.940
across the world.

00:33:16.940 --> 00:33:18.590
People are actively
moving to the cloud

00:33:18.590 --> 00:33:20.240
or have already moved
completely to the cloud.

00:33:20.240 --> 00:33:21.560
The number of tools
that you're using

00:33:21.560 --> 00:33:23.560
and the software you're
using to accomplish work

00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:26.040
is expanding every single day.

00:33:26.040 --> 00:33:28.880
And companies are trying
to react and figure out

00:33:28.880 --> 00:33:31.530
how they're going to deal
with this explosion of tools

00:33:31.530 --> 00:33:36.586
and this consumerization of
the enterprise software space.

00:33:36.586 --> 00:33:38.210
At Slack, we're taking
a very hard look

00:33:38.210 --> 00:33:39.320
at the shifting dynamic.

00:33:39.320 --> 00:33:42.380
And specifically how we can
get groups and teams of people

00:33:42.380 --> 00:33:44.180
fluidly, dynamically,
and efficiently

00:33:44.180 --> 00:33:46.765
working together, creating
a more transparent,

00:33:46.765 --> 00:33:48.890
and at the end of the day,
the most important thing

00:33:48.890 --> 00:33:51.350
is a more powerful
and a more efficient

00:33:51.350 --> 00:33:53.930
work environment for you,
the people who are actually

00:33:53.930 --> 00:33:55.550
accomplishing work.

00:33:55.550 --> 00:33:59.250
So our mission here is to make
people's working lives simpler,

00:33:59.250 --> 00:34:01.790
more pleasant, and more
productive at work.

00:34:01.790 --> 00:34:04.550
That is what we're trying to
do every single day at Slack.

00:34:04.550 --> 00:34:08.330
And on the platform team,
our specific team's goal

00:34:08.330 --> 00:34:10.460
is to combine the
tools and the software

00:34:10.460 --> 00:34:12.750
that you're using
every single day

00:34:12.750 --> 00:34:15.739
and bring them into the
place that the conversations

00:34:15.739 --> 00:34:20.179
around the work that's
happening is there already.

00:34:20.179 --> 00:34:22.909
So what that really looks like
in practice means that instead

00:34:22.909 --> 00:34:25.310
of having a contact switch
between multiple accounts,

00:34:25.310 --> 00:34:28.440
and multiple tabs, and multiple
browser windows, multiple Mac

00:34:28.440 --> 00:34:31.310
spaces, and maybe even
multiple different OS types,

00:34:31.310 --> 00:34:33.409
you can now pull
all of that software

00:34:33.409 --> 00:34:37.159
directly into Slack, seamlessly
integrating the conversations

00:34:37.159 --> 00:34:39.500
you are already having
with the work that you're

00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:41.020
attempting to get done.

00:34:41.020 --> 00:34:42.770
So what does that
really mean in practice?

00:34:42.770 --> 00:34:44.090
Say I'm a product manager.

00:34:44.090 --> 00:34:45.770
I'm having a conversation
with my sales

00:34:45.770 --> 00:34:47.019
team about a specific client.

00:34:47.019 --> 00:34:48.810
I don't meet with
clients every single day,

00:34:48.810 --> 00:34:50.570
so maybe I don't
have that context.

00:34:50.570 --> 00:34:52.429
Within the conversation,
I can directly

00:34:52.429 --> 00:34:54.969
pull all the information
about this client.

00:34:54.969 --> 00:34:57.510
Who they are, who their account
rep is, are we green, yellow,

00:34:57.510 --> 00:34:59.360
red with them, what's the
next conversation we're

00:34:59.360 --> 00:35:01.651
going to have with them,
directly into the conversation

00:35:01.651 --> 00:35:04.610
so I don't need to jump and
get disturbed and be pulled out

00:35:04.610 --> 00:35:06.350
of context and multitask.

00:35:06.350 --> 00:35:09.200
What if I want to check the
status of my support tickets

00:35:09.200 --> 00:35:11.720
because my fancy,
automated standing desk

00:35:11.720 --> 00:35:13.605
won't go up and down anymore?

00:35:13.605 --> 00:35:16.230
What if I wanted to reach out to
my help desk team and be like,

00:35:16.230 --> 00:35:17.660
hey, can we get someone
to come check this out?

00:35:17.660 --> 00:35:19.118
I can do that
directly within Slack

00:35:19.118 --> 00:35:21.230
without having to go
to another system,

00:35:21.230 --> 00:35:23.880
because there are enough
systems that are out there.

00:35:23.880 --> 00:35:25.520
And most importantly,
what I'm super

00:35:25.520 --> 00:35:27.147
excited to talk
about today, is what

00:35:27.147 --> 00:35:28.730
if you wanted to
share and collaborate

00:35:28.730 --> 00:35:31.550
on the docs and sheets
and slides that you

00:35:31.550 --> 00:35:33.110
have within Google Drive?

00:35:33.110 --> 00:35:34.430
What if you wanted to do that?

00:35:34.430 --> 00:35:36.930
Is it necessary to go somewhere
else to manage those things?

00:35:36.930 --> 00:35:37.460
No.

00:35:37.460 --> 00:35:39.209
We're really excited
with some of the work

00:35:39.209 --> 00:35:41.090
that we're doing, to
pull all of that work

00:35:41.090 --> 00:35:44.780
directly into Slack so that we
can connect the powerhouse that

00:35:44.780 --> 00:35:47.900
really is Google Drive with the
work that is happening inside

00:35:47.900 --> 00:35:48.650
of Slack.

00:35:48.650 --> 00:35:51.170
And it's the reason we're so
excited about Team Drives,

00:35:51.170 --> 00:35:54.800
because it takes Google
Drive beyond the domain

00:35:54.800 --> 00:35:57.057
and creates these
groups of people

00:35:57.057 --> 00:35:59.390
who are attempting to accomplish
and move work together.

00:35:59.390 --> 00:36:01.820
And more often than not,
those groups of people

00:36:01.820 --> 00:36:03.486
understand the
context with which

00:36:03.486 --> 00:36:05.360
those files need to be
shared and those files

00:36:05.360 --> 00:36:06.710
need to be discussed.

00:36:06.710 --> 00:36:09.290
So going into that more
micro view of those groups

00:36:09.290 --> 00:36:11.860
is something that's
super powerful.

00:36:11.860 --> 00:36:15.590
Now, Slack and G Suite, we've
been integrated since day one.

00:36:15.590 --> 00:36:18.670
So day one, Slack came out,
this has always been involved.

00:36:18.670 --> 00:36:21.830
We managed document importing,
indexing, search, and discovery

00:36:21.830 --> 00:36:23.030
directly into Slack.

00:36:23.030 --> 00:36:24.830
Simply by pasting
that link in there,

00:36:24.830 --> 00:36:27.140
it automatically becomes
discoverable and searchable

00:36:27.140 --> 00:36:30.500
within Slack already.

00:36:30.500 --> 00:36:32.970
But of course, we're
not stopping there.

00:36:32.970 --> 00:36:35.060
We have a very large
partnership with Google.

00:36:35.060 --> 00:36:37.820
We have a bunch of new things
that are coming out in 2017.

00:36:37.820 --> 00:36:40.359
Today I'm going to focus just
on the Team Drives use case.

00:36:40.359 --> 00:36:41.900
And the reason for
that is because we

00:36:41.900 --> 00:36:44.300
know at Google, who
takes security probably

00:36:44.300 --> 00:36:46.910
like more close to heart than
anyone else, and at Slack,

00:36:46.910 --> 00:36:48.950
that when teams come
together to work

00:36:48.950 --> 00:36:50.810
there's a whole
bunch of other issues

00:36:50.810 --> 00:36:52.567
that begin to become a problem.

00:36:52.567 --> 00:36:53.900
We're talking about permissions.

00:36:53.900 --> 00:36:54.860
We're talking about security.

00:36:54.860 --> 00:36:56.360
We're talking about
user management.

00:36:56.360 --> 00:36:59.300
We're talking about contractors
or freelancers who might come

00:36:59.300 --> 00:37:00.560
in temporarily join your team.

00:37:00.560 --> 00:37:02.720
These all become
massive problems,

00:37:02.720 --> 00:37:04.460
and as your company
grows and scales

00:37:04.460 --> 00:37:08.450
and as you begin to pull in
customer data and PII data,

00:37:08.450 --> 00:37:10.010
the escalation
policies are on all

00:37:10.010 --> 00:37:13.070
of these become more important
for us to be able to manage.

00:37:13.070 --> 00:37:16.040
So firstly, just
at the Drive level,

00:37:16.040 --> 00:37:19.250
you'll be able to provision new
Slack teams and users directly

00:37:19.250 --> 00:37:20.930
from Google Drive.

00:37:20.930 --> 00:37:24.590
What that means is your users,
your teams, your accounts,

00:37:24.590 --> 00:37:27.200
they all get completely
synchronized between these two

00:37:27.200 --> 00:37:29.150
disconnecting
platforms, making sure

00:37:29.150 --> 00:37:30.920
that the people who
are on one always

00:37:30.920 --> 00:37:33.380
exist [? and ?] the people
who are on the other.

00:37:33.380 --> 00:37:36.740
So if you're already managing
your user base through Google

00:37:36.740 --> 00:37:39.500
Drive, you won't have to involve
any other software applications

00:37:39.500 --> 00:37:40.970
to automatically
pull that into Slack.

00:37:40.970 --> 00:37:42.511
You can do that
directly from Google.

00:37:42.511 --> 00:37:44.300
It's super amazing.

00:37:44.300 --> 00:37:47.010
But if we zoom in on
that a little bit,

00:37:47.010 --> 00:37:50.300
and this is the thing that I'm
more excited to talk about,

00:37:50.300 --> 00:37:53.240
once that is done, you'll be
able to connect Slack channels

00:37:53.240 --> 00:37:55.492
directly into Team Drives.

00:37:55.492 --> 00:37:56.450
So what does that mean?

00:37:56.450 --> 00:37:58.400
Members of a channel
can automatically

00:37:58.400 --> 00:38:00.050
become members of
the Team Drive.

00:38:00.050 --> 00:38:02.180
Any file that you're
discussing and sharing

00:38:02.180 --> 00:38:03.770
with your colleagues
in that channel

00:38:03.770 --> 00:38:06.290
can automatically be uploaded
into your Team Drive,

00:38:06.290 --> 00:38:09.200
and then as people leave either
the company or the channel

00:38:09.200 --> 00:38:12.590
or the project, those files
will be maintained on that Team

00:38:12.590 --> 00:38:15.800
Drive so that you can
ensure that you never

00:38:15.800 --> 00:38:17.720
have any kind of document loss.

00:38:17.720 --> 00:38:20.840
Now, there is a lot of things
that we're talking about here.

00:38:20.840 --> 00:38:23.180
There's Google Drive,
there's Team Drives,

00:38:23.180 --> 00:38:25.670
there's Slack Teams, and
there are Slack Channels.

00:38:25.670 --> 00:38:28.760
So if we try to take that apart
and make this a little bit more

00:38:28.760 --> 00:38:31.880
real, what does
that actually mean?

00:38:31.880 --> 00:38:33.950
I'm sure that most
people here have

00:38:33.950 --> 00:38:36.310
an HR department, let's hope.

00:38:36.310 --> 00:38:39.140
And the HR department is
probably generally getting

00:38:39.140 --> 00:38:42.110
questions about what
benefits do I have,

00:38:42.110 --> 00:38:45.110
what health insurance can I
sign up for, where's the latest

00:38:45.110 --> 00:38:47.480
form for PTO days off.

00:38:47.480 --> 00:38:50.357
And I'm sure that this HR
team is constantly being like,

00:38:50.357 --> 00:38:51.440
oh, where is the document?

00:38:51.440 --> 00:38:52.160
Here's the document.

00:38:52.160 --> 00:38:53.740
Oh, I actually don't have
access to that document.

00:38:53.740 --> 00:38:55.198
Can you please
share that document?

00:38:55.198 --> 00:38:56.900
The number of times
that conversation

00:38:56.900 --> 00:38:59.660
back and forth happens in a
platform like Slack is just--

00:38:59.660 --> 00:39:01.970
the seconds that
are being wasted

00:39:01.970 --> 00:39:03.617
are moments that
your brain is having

00:39:03.617 --> 00:39:05.450
to switch contacts going
to this other thing

00:39:05.450 --> 00:39:08.840
and set up the permissions to
make sure this individual can

00:39:08.840 --> 00:39:10.410
get access to that file.

00:39:10.410 --> 00:39:12.950
Now, because we can sync
the channel directly

00:39:12.950 --> 00:39:14.510
with the Team
Drive, what it means

00:39:14.510 --> 00:39:17.150
is we can set read-only
permissions on this Team Drive.

00:39:17.150 --> 00:39:19.550
Anyone who accesses
the channel and is

00:39:19.550 --> 00:39:21.350
interested in the
Benefits questions

00:39:21.350 --> 00:39:22.970
automatically gets
read-only access

00:39:22.970 --> 00:39:24.970
to all of these files
in the Team Drive.

00:39:24.970 --> 00:39:26.650
It will be available
in their search.

00:39:26.650 --> 00:39:28.850
It will be available in
their Google Drive UI.

00:39:28.850 --> 00:39:31.520
And then when they leave
this HR Benefits channel,

00:39:31.520 --> 00:39:32.900
you can assume
that they probably

00:39:32.900 --> 00:39:35.180
don't have any HR Benefits
questions at the moment,

00:39:35.180 --> 00:39:37.610
so they'll automatically
be removed from the files

00:39:37.610 --> 00:39:39.390
that they don't need
to have access to.

00:39:39.390 --> 00:39:40.890
Now, that's an
interesting use case,

00:39:40.890 --> 00:39:45.250
but let's say we wanted to make
this a little bit more real.

00:39:45.250 --> 00:39:47.060
I'm sure that a lot
of companies are

00:39:47.060 --> 00:39:49.260
having really interesting
business development

00:39:49.260 --> 00:39:50.390
partnerships--

00:39:50.390 --> 00:39:51.890
conversations that
are happening.

00:39:51.890 --> 00:39:53.480
In fact, there are
probably a couple

00:39:53.480 --> 00:39:55.324
of companies in
this room today that

00:39:55.324 --> 00:39:56.990
are having conversations
with each other

00:39:56.990 --> 00:39:58.220
about potential partnerships.

00:39:58.220 --> 00:40:00.410
That's how businesses
move forward.

00:40:00.410 --> 00:40:02.090
But those partnerships
conversation

00:40:02.090 --> 00:40:04.260
needs to be kept really quiet.

00:40:04.260 --> 00:40:05.760
They need to be
kept very hush hush.

00:40:05.760 --> 00:40:08.570
And you want to have a very
strong amount of control

00:40:08.570 --> 00:40:11.132
in terms of who has
searched discovery

00:40:11.132 --> 00:40:13.340
access to these documents
and who can go and see them

00:40:13.340 --> 00:40:14.072
as well.

00:40:14.072 --> 00:40:16.280
So let's say we're talking
about the Slack and Google

00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:17.330
partnership.

00:40:17.330 --> 00:40:19.580
We could create a channel
that was specifically

00:40:19.580 --> 00:40:21.674
tied to this Slack and
Google relationship.

00:40:21.674 --> 00:40:23.090
We could create a
Team Drive where

00:40:23.090 --> 00:40:25.310
we have all of our legal
documents but also just

00:40:25.310 --> 00:40:27.110
like our product
development conversations

00:40:27.110 --> 00:40:28.370
in that Team Drive.

00:40:28.370 --> 00:40:31.940
And now as anyone who
joins the channel just

00:40:31.940 --> 00:40:34.477
called Google Partnerships
automatically gets access

00:40:34.477 --> 00:40:35.560
to all of those documents.

00:40:35.560 --> 00:40:37.640
It will appear within
their Drive UI.

00:40:37.640 --> 00:40:39.820
It will appear within
their Slack search.

00:40:39.820 --> 00:40:42.290
And if they were to
leave that project,

00:40:42.290 --> 00:40:43.710
we could automatically
say, well,

00:40:43.710 --> 00:40:45.209
anything that you
worked on, we want

00:40:45.209 --> 00:40:48.290
to keep those documents here,
we want new team members to be

00:40:48.290 --> 00:40:50.600
able to discover those files.

00:40:50.600 --> 00:40:52.100
But you're no longer
on the project,

00:40:52.100 --> 00:40:54.410
so your access
should be revoked.

00:40:54.410 --> 00:40:57.770
All of that can
now happen as easy

00:40:57.770 --> 00:41:01.910
as it is to join or
leave a Slack channel.

00:41:01.910 --> 00:41:04.086
Some absolutely amazing
things with Team Drive.

00:41:04.086 --> 00:41:05.960
I guess the thing that
we're excited with not

00:41:05.960 --> 00:41:08.150
only is that Team Drive
has been announced,

00:41:08.150 --> 00:41:10.534
but that all of those APIs
around those permissions

00:41:10.534 --> 00:41:12.200
and security settings
that we would need

00:41:12.200 --> 00:41:14.366
to be able to implement
something on the Slack side,

00:41:14.366 --> 00:41:15.780
Google's opened up.

00:41:15.780 --> 00:41:19.380
And that amount of control
is just incredibly powerful.

00:41:19.380 --> 00:41:22.280
We have a bunch of things
going live in 2017 together.

00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:24.350
We're really excited for
the Team Drives work.

00:41:24.350 --> 00:41:27.051
Congratulations, Steve and Hodie
for going into [? GA ?] today.

00:41:27.051 --> 00:41:28.050
And thank you very much.

00:41:33.554 --> 00:41:34.720
STEVE BAZYL: Thanks, Salman.

00:41:34.720 --> 00:41:37.540
To recap, Team
Drives is expanding

00:41:37.540 --> 00:41:39.910
Drive with new capabilities
to better serve

00:41:39.910 --> 00:41:42.010
the needs of teams.

00:41:42.010 --> 00:41:44.350
Apps that wish to
use Team Drives do

00:41:44.350 --> 00:41:45.580
need to make some changes.

00:41:45.580 --> 00:41:47.230
And as you've seen,
we have partners

00:41:47.230 --> 00:41:48.896
who've already gone
through this partner

00:41:48.896 --> 00:41:51.130
to add support for Team
Drives to their products.

00:41:51.130 --> 00:41:55.540
And starting today, the APIs are
available for you to integrate

00:41:55.540 --> 00:41:58.870
with your products as well.

00:41:58.870 --> 00:42:00.550
HODIE MEYERS: Yeah,
as [INAUDIBLE] said,

00:42:00.550 --> 00:42:01.800
he mentioned this
morning in the keynote,

00:42:01.800 --> 00:42:04.590
there are a lot more exciting
things coming to Drive today.

00:42:04.590 --> 00:42:06.420
So I encourage everyone
interested in Drive

00:42:06.420 --> 00:42:09.501
to also attend the talk
this afternoon at 1:20.

00:42:09.501 --> 00:42:12.000
It's called "Google Drive-- the
enterprise-ready alternative

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:14.652
to on-prem fileshares and
legacy content management."

00:42:14.652 --> 00:42:15.860
STEVE BAZYL: It's a mouthful.

00:42:15.860 --> 00:42:18.750
HODIE MEYERS: It's over there
in [? Salon ?] 8, the big room.

00:42:18.750 --> 00:42:21.510
And I think will be
very exciting too

00:42:21.510 --> 00:42:22.980
if you interested in Drive.

